Snow scattered on the edge of the screen
Why didn't it snow when I was home? I say
Home
A cold, empty place I no longer know, buried in the blanket of night. 
My mother does all the shoveling. as usual. Perhaps she dreams of eternal spring in the southland. 
Perhaps I should have stayed in the city that never sleeps, with the whole world at my feet. 
Wait--the city still doesn't sleep
but there is no snow here. 
They say it's winter now, yet I've never worn a hoodie. 
Where am I, really?
The place that speaks my mother's tongue 
let me see it when I'm young.

